  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "The molecular formula of ethane is $\\mathrm{C}_{2} \\mathrm{H}_{\\mathrm{6}}$ To get its fourth homologue, we have to add\r\n$$\r\n\\begin{array}{r}\r\n4 \\times \\mathrm{CH}_{2}=\\mathrm{C}_{4} \\mathrm{H}_{8} \\text { to it. } \\\\\r\n\\mathrm{C}_{2} \\mathrm{H}_{6}+\\mathrm{C}_4 \\mathrm{H}_{8}=\\mathrm{C}_6 \\mathrm{H}_{14}\r\n\\end{array}\r\n$$\r\n$\\mathrm{C}_{6} \\mathrm{H}_{14}$ is the molecular formula of hexane. Thus, hexane is the fourth homologue of ethane.",
    "image": null
  },
